    "beyond": {
      "word": "BEYOND",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "On the further side of; in the same direction as, and further on or away than. Beyond that flaming hill. G. Fletcher.",
          "partOfSpeech": "preposition"
        },
        {
          "text": "At a place or time not yet reached; before. A thing beyond us, even before our death. Pope.",
          "partOfSpeech": "preposition"
        },
        {
          "text": "Past, out of the reach or sphere of; further than; greater than; as, the patient was beyond medical aid; beyond one's strength.",
          "partOfSpeech": "preposition"
        },
        {
          "text": "In a degree or amount exceeding or surpassing; proceeding to a greater degree than; above, as in dignity, excellence, or quality of any kind. \"Beyond expectation.\" Barrow. Beyond any of the great men of my country. Sir P. Sidney. Beyond sea. (Law) See under Sea. else; hence, in a bed sense, to deceive or circumvent. That no man go beyond and defraud his brother in any matter. 1 Thess. iv. 6.",
          "partOfSpeech": "preposition"
        },
        {
          "text": "Further away; at a distance; yonder. Lo, where beyond he lyeth languishing. Spenser.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adverb"
        }
      ],
